[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
Below is a **complete, working pattern** for a MapLibre GL JS v6 app that

1. loads a **PMTiles** file (a single-file container of vector tiles) and  
2. draws a **line** layer from one of the source-layers inside that file.

The code works whether you are loading MapLibre from a CDN **or** from a bundler (Vite, webpack, etc.).  
All of the v5-to-v6 breaking-change points are highlighted so you won’t hit the usual “it used to work” errors.

---

## 1️⃣ Install the two packages (if you use a bundler)

```bash
npm i maplibre-gl@^6 pmtiles
# or with Yarn / pnpm
```

> **NOTE** – `maplibre-gl` v6 is **ESM-only**. There is no default export and there is no CommonJS `require()` support.  
> If you are still on a plain `<script>` tag, skip the bundler steps and go straight to the CDN example in section 2.

---

## 2️⃣ CDN-only (no bundler) – the simplest way to try it out

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>PMTiles + MapLibre v6</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  // 1️⃣ Import the ESM build from the CDN
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';
  // 2️⃣ Import the PMTiles helper (also ESM)
  import { PMTiles } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pmtiles@2.7.0/dist/index.mjs';

  // 3️⃣ Register the custom protocol that lets MapLibre fetch from a .pmtiles file
  const pmtiles = new PMTiles('https://YOUR_DOMAIN/path/to/your-data.pmtiles');
  pmtiles.addProtocol();               // registers the "pmtiles://" fetch handler

  // 4️⃣ Create the map (no need for setWorkerUrl() when using a CDN)
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json', // any base style you like
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2
  });

  // 5️⃣ When the base style is ready, add the PMTiles source + line layer
  map.on('style.load', () => {
    // ---- vector source that points at the PMTiles file ----
    map.addSource('my-pmtiles', {
      type: 'vector',
      // The URL must use the "pmtiles://" scheme; the part after the scheme
      // must be **exactly** the same string you passed to the PMTiles ctor.
      url: 'pmtiles://https://YOUR_DOMAIN/path/to/your-data.pmtiles'
    });

    // ---- line layer that draws from a source-layer inside the PMTiles ----
    map.addLayer({
      id: 'my-lines',
      type: 'line',
      source: 'my-pmtiles',
      // Replace this with the actual source-layer name that lives inside the .pmtiles file
      'source-layer': 'roads',          // <-- e.g. "roads", "railways", etc.
      layout: {
        'line-cap': 'round',
        'line-join': 'round'
      },
      paint: {
        'line-color': '#ff6600',
        'line-width': 2,
        'line-opacity': 0.9
      }
    });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**What changed from v5?**

| v5 pattern | v6 replacement |
|------------|----------------|
| `import maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'` | `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'` (or named imports) |
| `<script src="…/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>` | `<script type="module"> import … from '…/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs'; </script>` |
| `require('maplibre-gl')` | Not supported – use dynamic `import()` if you must stay in CommonJS |
| `styleimagemissing` → `addImage()` | Use `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver()` (not needed for this example) |
| `map.transform` | Use public getters (`map.getZoom()`, `map.getCenter()`, …) |
| `MapDataEvent` | Use `MapSourceDataEvent | MapStyleDataEvent` (not needed here) |
| Bundled apps → `setWorkerUrl()` | **Not needed** for CDN-only; see section 4 for bundler setup |

---

## 3️⃣ Bundler setup (Vite, webpack, esbuild, Rollup, etc.)

Below is a minimal **Vite** example; the same idea works for other bundlers – just call `setWorkerUrl()` once before creating the map.

### `src/main.ts` (or `main.js`)

```ts
// 1️⃣ Import the public API (named or namespace)
import { Map, setWorkerUrl } from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';

// 2️⃣ Import the worker URL – Vite’s `?worker&url` query makes the worker a separate file
import workerUrl from 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?worker&url';

// 3️⃣ Register the worker (required for any bundler build)
setWorkerUrl(workerUrl);

// 4️⃣ Import the PMTiles helper (ESM)
import { PMTiles } from 'pmtiles';

// 5️⃣ Register the custom protocol
const pmtiles = new PMTiles('/data/your-data.pmtiles'); // relative to your public folder
pmtiles.addProtocol();

// 6️⃣ Create the map
const map = new Map({
  container: 'map',               // <-- a <div id="map"></div> in your HTML
  style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json',
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2
});

// 7️⃣ Add source + line layer once the style is loaded
map.on('style.load', () => {
  map.addSource('my-pmtiles', {
    type: 'vector',
    url: 'pmtiles://data/your-data.pmtiles' // matches the URL you gave to PMTiles ctor
  });

  map.addLayer({
    id: 'my-lines',
    type: 'line',
    source: 'my-pmtiles',
    'source-layer': 'roads',          // <-- change to the actual layer name
    layout: {
      'line-cap': 'round',
      'line-join': 'round'
    },
    paint: {
      'line-color': '#0066ff',
      'line-width': 3,
      'line-opacity': 0.8
    }
  });
});
```

### `index.html`

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>PMTiles + MapLibre (Vite)</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; inset:0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="map"></div>
  <script type="module" src="/src/main.ts"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

**Key bundler-specific notes**

| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| **Worker not found** (`Failed to load worker script`) | Call `setWorkerUrl()` with the URL you import (`?worker&url` for Vite, `new URL('…/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs', import.meta.url).toString()` for webpack/rollup). |
| **`require('maplibre-gl')` error** | Use ESM imports as shown; if you must stay in CommonJS, do `const { Map } = await import('maplibre-gl');`. |
| **Missing default export** | Use named/namespace imports (`import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'` or `import { Map } from 'maplibre-gl'`). |
| **`styleimagemissing` no longer resolves** | Not needed for a simple line layer; if you need dynamic icons, use `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(...)`. |
| **`map.transform`** | Use the public getters (`map.getZoom()`, `map.getCenter()`, etc.). |
| **`MapDataEvent`** | Use the union types (`MapSourceDataEvent | MapStyleDataEvent`) if you type-annotate event handlers. |

---

## 4️⃣ Quick checklist before you run

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| **MapLibre version** | `npm list maplibre-gl` → should be `6.x` |
| **PMTiles version** | `npm list pmtiles` → any recent 2.x release |
| **Import style** | No default import, only `import * as maplibregl` or named imports |
| **Worker URL** | `setWorkerUrl()` called **once** *before* `new Map()` (bundler only) |
| **Protocol registration** | `new PMTiles(...).addProtocol();` executed **before** `map.addSource` |
| **Source URL** | Starts with `pmtiles://` and matches the string you passed to `PMTiles` |
| **Source-layer name** | Verify the exact name inside the .pmtiles file (use `pmtiles inspect` or a viewer) |
| **CSP / CSP-compatible** | If you serve the page with a strict CSP, remember to allow `script-src` for the worker URL (`blob:` or the exact path). |

---

